# Normalise to LF in the repository; the J-Link command scripts that the server
# generates at runtime are written with CRLF in code (see src/jlink.ts) and are
# never committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendor documentation copied from the SEGGER J-Link installation (docs/vendor/).
# These are byte-for-byte copies of SEGGER's files and their SHA-256 hashes are
# recorded in docs/reference/vendor-manifest.md, so git must not rewrite their
# line endings. -text disables all end-of-line conversion; -diff keeps the large
# generated text files out of diffs. NOTICE.md, which is ours, stays normal text.
docs/vendor/*.pdf binary
docs/vendor/*.txt -text -diff
docs/vendor/*.xml -text -diff
docs/vendor/*.html -text -diff

# Trellis: append-only developer journals should merge cleanly across
# parallel sessions/worktrees — each session only appends a new block, so
# there is nothing to actually conflict on.
#
# Do NOT add a rule for workspace/*/index.md here — it is fully regenerated
# every session, so a real conflict there is expected and safe to resolve by
# picking either side (task state lives in task.json, not index.md). See
# .trellis/spec/cli/backend/directory-structure.md for details.
.trellis/workspace/*/journal-*.md merge=union
